    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `digitSum` function that meets your requirements:\n\n```python\ndef digitSum(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Task\n    Write a function string takes as input and it returns the sum of of the upper \n    characters' ASCII codes only.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isupper():\n            total += ord(char)\n\n    return total\n```\n\nThis function iterates through the each character character in the input string, checks if it is uppercase is uppercase, and if it is, then it adds the ASCII value of the character to the a running total. Finally, it returns the total sum of the ASCII values of the uppercase characters.",
